        "heading": "We know that when your skin is uncomfortable, life is, too.",
        "body": "<p><strong>Relieving flare-ups starts with understanding the underlying condition and its triggers.</strong></p><p>Eczema and dermatitis are terms often used interchangeably to describe inflammatory skin conditions. According to DermNet, <a href=\"https://dermnetnz.org/topics/dermatitis\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"about 1 in 5 people\">about 1 in 5 people</a> experience eczema or dermatitis at some point in their lives. These conditions can cause itching and discomfort, but they are not contagious.</p><p>Eczema can <a href=\"https://www.aad.org/public/diseases/eczema/types/atopic-dermatitis/symptoms\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"come and go for years\">come and go for years</a>, the American Academy of Dermatology notes, but treatments can help manage symptoms and prevent flare-ups. Some forms of contact dermatitis can also resolve completely with appropriate treatment and avoidance of the triggering substance.</p>",
